#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:5
#: f50ef748d877488c9b97feccbc4adf14
msgid "Pozyx for Non-GPS Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:9
#: a2a750d7edb24762afdc52ca307651b7
msgid "This article explains how a `Pozyx <https://www.pozyx.io/>`__ system based on the `DWM1000 <http://www.decawave.com/products/dwm1000-module>`__ can be used as a short-range substitute for a GPS allowing position control modes like Loiter, PosHold, RTL, Auto indoors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:15
#: 32b3c4511d944d4cb47bc1f55468716a
msgid "Required Hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:17
#: 6e75be851be040d9a19c5ab8762fc6f9
msgid "4 `Pozyx anchors <https://www.pozyx.io/store/detail/5>`__ and 1 `Pozyx tag <https://www.pozyx.io/store/detail/4>`__.  Note the `Ready to Localize <https://www.pozyx.io/store/detail/2>`__ or `Developer Kits <https://www.pozyx.io/store/detail/3>`__ are more economical than buying individual tags and anchors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:18
#: 68ae77e1351a47f7b583cc1f0cd72b91
msgid "one `Arduino Uno R2 or R3 <https://www.arduino.cc/en/Main/ArduinoBoardUno>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:19
#: aa0338e058ad4fc7b0cb29257405d58c
msgid "4 `portable chargers <https://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_noss_2?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=portable+charger&rh=i%3Aaps%2Ck%3Aportable+charger>`__ with type A USB ports to power the anchors (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:20
#: 13f0db2d86b140c08cd43c870f51b485
msgid "4 `tripods <https://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_noss_1?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=tripod&rh=i%3Aaps%2Ck%3Atripod>`__ to mount the anchors (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:23
#: 20ab61c21ed540398a74c3e3e44440fe
msgid "Placing the anchors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:25
#: e349dc2a2b30440496797a10aa2120b1
msgid "The anchors should be placed in a rectangular shape.  The anchor with the lowest ID (IDs are printed in hexadecimal on each device) will act as the \"origin\" and should be placed at the lower-left corner of the rectangle.  Each of the remaining three anchors should be placed in a corner so that the anchor IDs increase as you travel an \"N\" pattern within the rectangle.  The configuration is slightly simpler if the line from the origin anchor to the 2nd anchor is due North but it is not required as the :ref:`BCN_ORIENT_YAW <BCN_ORIENT_YAW>` parameter can be used to account this difference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:31
#: 16168636382242cdae0fda1283ed2ac0
msgid "Preparing the tag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:36
#: 84933466002e460e89acf9ede20cabc9
msgid "connect one of the autopilot's telemetry connections to the UNO.  Telem1 is shown above but any SERIAL port will work equally well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:37
#: d05ca9b2682a473c854870b441d613c3
msgid "autopilot's UART port GND should be connected to one of the UNO's GND pins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:38
#: dbbf860c50bf4ccda46f144b429e7cdd
msgid "autopilot's UART port TX should be connected to the UNO's pin 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:39
#: c887670d24174dc59624df9addefc3f7
msgid "autopilot's UART port RX should be connected to the UNO's pin 11."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:40
#: 84f85cf171084b9dbde1057fec96242b
msgid "autopilot's UART port VCC may be connected to the UNO's 5V connector to provide power to the Uno/Pozyx from the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:42
#: f3b1a4c5ce3d4fdeb9b36b98dabae041
msgid "The Arduino IDE should be used to load `IndoorLoiter sketch <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/Pozyx/IndoorLoiter/IndoorLoiter.ino>`__ onto the Uno after first changing the anchor tags `found here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/Pozyx/IndoorLoiter/IndoorLoiter.ino#L12>`__ to match the IDs of the tags in your setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:44
#: 54cf4909e2d04277836adac9b2247c1a
msgid "At this point you may wish to test the tag's ability to communicate with the tags by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:46
#: 179a5b6e84924ad7bfc2d55b728c0664
msgid "powering on all the anchors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:47
#: 47798b2c7bcb4a908eb3ec86b899ad05
msgid "connect the UNO's Type B USB to your PC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:48
#: 8495b54705da430aac967173e6eb88db
msgid "connect with the Arduino IDE's serial monitor (set to baud 115200) and check no \"Beacon Configuration failed\" messages appear.  If they do, check that the IDs have been set correctly in the IndoorLoiter2.ino sketch (above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:50
#: 1ba32fb4f7c8471a9afb2b57d9d4853a
msgid "Mount the Pozyx tag on the top of the Arduino Uno and then mount on the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:53
#: 31bec0bb46b449149a359b8fb0e99eac
msgid "Configuration through the Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:55
#: 020ac01783e14377b9027c26b3a7d646
msgid "Connect with a Ground Station and set the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:57
#: 65d5d10d18eb4d6c9c4278bd49c265fa
msgid "set :ref:`BCN_TYPE <BCN_TYPE>` to 1 (means using Pozyx system)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:58
#: 7a7b330a0d7e43a7842eba3bffbfb51f
msgid "set :ref:`BCN_LATITUDE <BCN_LATITUDE>`, :ref:`BCN_LONGITUDE <BCN_LONGITUDE>` and :ref:`BCN_ALT <BCN_ALT>` to match your actual location.  Getting these values exactly correct is not particularly important although getting it close is required in order for the compass's declination to be correctly looked up from the small database held within ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:59
#: 0336610d21674e95affb19b51ae84d5e
msgid "set :ref:`BCN_ORIENT_YAW <BCN_ORIENT_YAW>` to the heading from the origin anchor to the 2nd anchor.  One way to capture this value is to stand at the origin holding the vehicle so that its nose points towards the second beacon.  Read the vehicle's heading from the HUD and enter this value into :ref:`BCN_ORIENT_YAW <BCN_ORIENT_YAW>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:60
#: e76142dd24654dbf903132f229c1510a
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSXY <EK3_SRC1_POSXY>` to 4 (Beacon)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:61
#: 75c03c3bf0af4dbd863731a98e90b440
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELXY <EK3_SRC1_VELXY>` to 0 (None)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:62
#: d76d0003e8f64427b327441aabf9e753
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELZ <EK3_SRC1_VELZ>` to 0 (None)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:63
#: 6350399a28b9481cba04fe71e2f7a52c
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSZ<EK3_SRC1_POSZ>` to  4 (Beacon)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:64
#: eaee2ab497de4fdab415150d53e36038
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_YAW<EK3_SRC1_YAW>` to 1 (Compass) since a compass is required for use with this device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:65
#: 4fe49456b5b04c13877a3508f952a381
msgid "set :ref:`ARMING_SKIPCHK <ARMING_SKIPCHK>` to 8 to disable the GPS arming check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:66
#: cfc0b11e4e1f43008b760612adcf87d9
msgid "set :ref:`SERIAL1_BAUD <SERIAL1_BAUD>` to 115 to set SERIAL1 port's baud rate to 115200 (if using a different SERIAL port set its baud rate to 115, instead)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:67
#: 8c29876f851c425280cd7478e5bca52f
msgid "set :ref:`SERIAL1_PROTOCOL <SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>` to 13 (Beacon) to enable reading the IndoorLoiter2 protocol (If using a different port, set its protocol to 13 instead)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:68
#: 73bf4924be58447ab0ab8cda70af755f
msgid "set :ref:`BRD_SER1_RTSCTS <BRD_SER1_RTSCTS>` to 0 to ensure telem1 does not use flow control (If using Telem2 set :ref:`BRD_SER2_RTSCTS <BRD_SER2_RTSCTS>` instead, not required if using a SERIAL port without flow control)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:71
#: 47a2dce3688c4a3281974eeee0b52d9e
msgid "Ground Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:73
#: 09d2155be0864d349c97186a83bfea74
msgid "Connect the Autopilot to a ground station.  You may need to connect the Lipo battery as well because some computers are unable to provide enough power through their USB port for the combined autopilot+Pozyx+Uno."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:74
#: 8b0354977c9143a185d7be87c43b0ef7
msgid "Press the UNO's white or red reset button which can be found next to the USB port (see image above)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:75
#: a8fef273087e4a149e0222119fe4b80f
msgid "After about 1 minute the vehicle's position should jump to the latitude, longitude you input during the configuration step (above).  If it does not, connect a USB cable to the UNO's USB port and open the Arduino IDE's serial monitor and look for errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:76
#: 56259e49a49b49679509dae76d8dbe2e
msgid "Check that the vehicle's position is relatively stable (i.e. moving around less than one meter)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:77
#: 7730b52381d24e3e925ed26ebaf5bc24
msgid "Walk the vehicle around between the anchors and ensure that its position on the map updates correctly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:80
#: 219500c482bf4ebdbaaf4d9b6bea499a
msgid "Flight testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:82
#: 30a25678a50940abb2c851a15df27e40
msgid "Setup the transmitter with Stabilize, AltHold and Loiter flight modes. Take off in AltHold mode and maintain a stable hover. Switch to Loiter but be ready to switch back to AltHold or Stabilize if the vehicle's position or altitude becomes unstable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:87
#: 30f34f5a3a11445a98109a6452442854
msgid "DataFlash logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pozyx.rst:89
#: df088c9395174f05aabf8ec76955fb03
msgid "The distance to the beacons can be found in the dataflash log's BCN message's D0, D1, D2, D3 fields."
msgstr ""

